<title>AUSTRALIA: Coles Myer shares dip after analysts tour.</title>
<headline>Coles Myer shares dip after analysts tour.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The shares of Australia's largest retailer, Coles Myer Ltd, opened weaker on Thursday after retail analysts were given a tour of the group's operations on Wednesday.</p>
<p>At 10.30 a.m (0030 GMT), Coles shares were 14 cents down at A$6.16 on turnover of 1.14 million shares.</p>
<p>&quot;Yesterday was the annual tour the company hosts for analysts,&quot; a Melbourne-based dealer said.</p>
<p>&quot;It's quite possible that answers to analyst questions at the end of the tour has prompted some negative reaction this morning,&quot; the dealer said.</p>
<p>-- Melbourne Bureau 61-3 9286-1435</p>
</text>
